.TH "JEDI" "1" "Sep 04, 2026" "0.20.0" "Jedi"
.SH "نام (NAME)"
jedi \- Jedi Documentation
[image: GitHub stars]
[image]
 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:davidhalter/\:jedi>[image: The percentage of open issues and pull requests]
[image]
 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:davidhalter/\:jedi/\:issues>[image: The resolution time is the median time an issue or pull request stays open.]
[image]
 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:davidhalter/\:jedi/\:issues>[image: Tests]
[image]
 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:davidhalter/\:jedi/\:actions>[image: Coverage status]
[image]
 \%<https://\:coveralls\:.io/\:r/\:davidhalter/\:jedi>[image: PyPI Downloads]
[image]
 \%<https://\:pepy\:.tech/\:project/\:jedi>
.sp
Github Repository \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:davidhalter/\:jedi>
.sp
Jedi is a static analysis tool for Python that is typically used in
IDEs/editors plugins. Jedi has a focus on autocompletion and goto
functionality. Other features include refactoring, code search and finding
references.
.sp
Jedi has a simple API to work with. There is a reference implementation as a
VIM\-Plugin \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:davidhalter/\:jedi-vim>\&. Autocompletion in your
REPL is also possible, IPython uses it natively and for the CPython REPL you
can install it. Jedi is well tested and bugs should be rare.
.sp
Here\(aqs a simple example of the autocompletion feature:
.sp
.EX
>>> import jedi
>>> source = \(aq\(aq\(aq
\&... import json
\&... json.lo\(aq\(aq\(aq
>>> script = jedi.Script(source, path=\(aqexample.py\(aq)
>>> script
<Script: \(aqexample.py\(aq ...>
>>> completions = script.complete(3, len(\(aqjson.lo\(aq))
>>> completions
[<Completion: load>, <Completion: loads>]
>>> print(completions[0].complete)
ad
>>> print(completions[0].name)
load
.EE
.sp
Autocompletion can for example look like this in jedi\-vim:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 2.5
[image]
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.SH DOCS
.SS Using Jedi
.sp
Jedi can be used with a variety of plugins,
language servers and other software.
It is also possible to use Jedi in the Python shell or with IPython\&.
.sp
Below you can also find a list of recipes for type hinting\&.
.SS Language Servers
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
jedi\-language\-server \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pappasam/\:jedi-language-server>
.IP \(bu 2
python\-language\-server \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:palantir/\:python-language-server> (currently unmaintained)
.IP \(bu 2
python\-lsp\-server \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:python-lsp/\:python-lsp-server> (fork from python\-language\-server)
.IP \(bu 2
anakin\-language\-server \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:muffinmad/\:anakin-language-server>
.UNINDENT
